# Reopen-blank — ① BASELINE (before this session): no restore

> The actual starting point — what the system did before any of this work. This is the bug as reported.
>
> Progression: **① baseline (this doc) → ② rejected client attempt → ③ shipped server design.**

## Idea in one line
**Nothing is saved.** Hibernate throws the output away; reopen just restarts the CLI and you stare at a **blank screen** until it finishes re-printing.

## What exists — only an in-memory buffer that dies on hibernate

```mermaid
flowchart TB
  subgraph CLIENT["CLIENT (renderer)"]
    XT["xterm<br/>(blank on reopen<br/>until reprint lands)"]
  end
  subgraph SERVER["MAIN (terminal still in-process)"]
    PTY["PTY"] --> RB["RingBuffer<br/>(in memory ONLY)"]
    RB -. "freed on hibernate" .-> X["✗ gone"]
  end
  SERVER -->|"live output only"| CLIENT
  classDef bad fill:#5b2330,stroke:#e0506a,color:#ffd7df;
  class X,RB bad
```

There is no persistence anywhere — not on the client, not on disk. The history lives only in RAM, and hibernation frees it.

## Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant U as User
  participant C as Client (xterm)
  participant S as Server (PTY)
  rect rgb(48,40,42)
  note over C,S: Hibernate
  S->>S: kill PTY + free RingBuffer (history lost)
  end
  rect rgb(48,40,42)
  note over C,S: Reopen
  U->>C: click Reopen
  S->>S: spawn CLI --resume
  Note over C: BLANK SCREEN (no spinner)
  Note over C,S: ...seconds while CLI boots + re-prints...
  S-->>C: reprint transcript (live)
  C->>C: finally shows content
  end
```

## Why it's a problem
- 🔴 **Blank, no loading state.** The overlay clears in a microtask, but the resumed transcript takes seconds → you watch a blank background.
- 🔴 **Nothing to fall back on.** The buffer is gone; the *only* way to get content back is to wait for the CLI to re-stream it.

➡️ The rest of the session was about fixing this. First attempt put the fix on the client (② — rejected); the shipped fix puts it on the server (③).
